hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27639","Haddathana Abu Amir, he said: Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Habibah, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah al-Ashhali narrated to me from Umm Amir bint Yazid, a woman among those who pledged, that she brought the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a bone in the mosque of Banu so-and-so, and he ate from it, then he stood and prayed and did not perform ablution."
